* PMOS cascode whose cascode rail is generated by a stacked diode branch
* This is the polarity complement of self_biased_cascode: no ideal source
* fixes either PMOS gate rail, so the PMOS model selects the operating point.
<MODEL_SETUP>
Vdd vdd 0 <VDD>
Vbp bp 0 <BODY_P>
Rrefp pc 0 <CASCODE_BIAS_LOAD>
<P_PREFIX>p_casdio pc pc pb bp <P_DEVICE>
<P_PREFIX>p_lodio pb pb vdd bp <P_DEVICE>
Voutp dp 0 <CASCODE_OUT>
<P_PREFIX>p_lo px pb vdd bp <P_DEVICE>
<P_PREFIX>p_hi dp pc px bp <P_DEVICE>
<OUTPUT_LOAD>
.temp <TEMP>
<ANALYSIS>
.end
